> Congratulations!
> Now that you're mostly through, what's your opinion on role difficulty?

1) Easy roles
I think all the combat classes are easy: Barbarian, Knight and
Samurai. Strong in the early game, strong in the late game.
Spellcasting is strictly optional.

2) Somewhat easy
Monks are rather easy early on, but they have challenging quest and
the late game loses it's luster compared to the above. Rogues have
rather easy early game due to backstab bonus, but again their quest is
challenging.

3) Intermediate
Caveman are harder version of Barbarians. Priests are somewhat weaker
early on. I had quite some trouble with Rangers, no good melee weapon
early on, and I could get the hang of bow.

4) Challenge roles
Archeologists are weak early on, before they get dwarvish mattock,
though they have some unique advantages; they have powerful late game,
though. Healers were the most difficult role for me: no good weapon,
terrible AC, weak; late game is fairly powerful, though.



